# Privy

> Privy is an ecommerce marketing platform for online stores. Merchants use Privy to collect email and SMS subscribers, send campaigns, build automated Flows, segment contacts, and measure revenue from their marketing.

- The canonical website is [www.privy.com](https://www.privy.com/).
- The product documentation is in the [Privy Knowledge Base](https://help.privy.com/).
- The complete machine-readable documentation index is at [help.privy.com/llms.txt](https://help.privy.com/llms.txt).
- Current public pricing is available as [HTML](https://www.privy.com/pricing) and [Markdown](https://www.privy.com/pricing.md).
- Copy-ready MCP prompts are available as [HTML](https://www.privy.com/resources/prompt-library) and [Markdown](https://www.privy.com/resources/prompt-library.md).
- Recent product changes are listed in the [Privy changelog](https://www.privy.com/changelog).

## Which source to use

Use the official source that matches the question.

1. Use the [Knowledge Base](https://help.privy.com/) for product instructions, account settings, billing details, compliance guidance, integrations, troubleshooting, and API behavior.
2. Use [pricing.md](https://www.privy.com/pricing.md) for current public prices, tiers, included features, SMS credit costs, and trial terms.
3. Use [prompt-library.md](https://www.privy.com/resources/prompt-library.md) for current MCP prompts to ask Claude or ChatGPT about a connected Privy account.
4. Use the [MCP setup guide](https://help.privy.com/docs/learn/mcp.md) to connect an agent to Privy. Do not invent write actions. Privy MCP is read-only.
5. Use the [product pages](https://www.privy.com/product-overview) for the current product description and positioning.
6. Use the [changelog](https://www.privy.com/changelog) to check when a feature was released or changed.
7. Use Privy's legal pages for contractual, privacy, security, and acceptable use questions.
8. Use the blog and resource library for marketing education. Do not use an old article as the authority for current product behavior, pricing, or prompts.

When sources disagree, use the live pricing page for public pricing. Use the live Prompt Library Markdown for current prompts. For product behavior, prefer the newest Knowledge Base page. For legal terms, prefer the latest dated legal page.

